{# =====================================================================
   Template: node_plan_global  (Module M05 — Hierarchical Planning Cascade, Level 1)
   Rendered by prompts/prompt_loader.py (StrictUndefined, autoescape=False).

   The harness owns a bounded deliberation loop; this prompt is re-rendered each
   turn. The model returns exactly ONE PlannerAction (Data_Structures §1.4) per
   turn; the harness validates it and decides whether a finalize is accepted.

   Expected context variables (ALL are required — StrictUndefined; omitting any
   raises). The node supplies the base-context group; the decider
   (fsm/planning_node_support.make_planner_decider) supplies the loop-state group
   every turn.

   Base context (node_plan_global supplies):
     genre             : str        — book genre / category.
     target_word_count : int|str    — total word-count target (Density Model input).
     premise_seed      : str        — the user's brief / creative seed for the book.
     world_rules       : list[str]  — parsed world/setting rules (may be empty).
     existing_arcs      : list       — already-planned arcs, for a continuation pass
                                       (empty list for a fresh book).

   Loop state (the planner decider supplies each turn):
     loop_index          : int       — 0-based deliberation turn index.
     current_plan        : dict|None  — the working draft global plan, or None.
     tool_results        : list[dict] — accumulated results of permitted tool calls.
     compiled_constraints: dict       — compiled annotation package; reads
                                        .hard_annotations and .soft_preferences.
     last_validation     : obj|None   — last harness validation (.passes,
                                        .failed_checks), or None on the first turn.
     last_refusal        : dict|None  — the most recent refused tool request, or None.
   ===================================================================== #}
<planner_task level="global">

  <role>
    You are the Global Planner for a long-form novel. You own Level 1 of a
    five-level planning cascade (Global -> Arc -> Chapter -> Scene -> Beat). Your
    job is to establish the master timeline and thematic boundaries for the entire
    book — never prose, never scene or beat detail. You propose; an automated
    harness validates every proposal and decides whether it is accepted.
  </role>

  <planning_objective>
    Produce a coherent global plan that a downstream arc planner can expand. A
    complete global plan must specify:
      - premise / logline: a one- to two-sentence statement of the story.
      - central_conflict: the single driving conflict the whole book turns on.
      - ending_target: the intended end-state / resolution the book builds toward.
      - major_promises: the major promises the opening makes to the reader, each
        paired with its intended payoff (where/how it is honored).
      - arcs: the ordered set of arcs that cover the whole story from premise to
        ending_target, each with a clear narrative function and a rough word
        allocation. Size the arcs with a "density" judgement — allot more words to
        arcs carrying more subplot and character complexity — so the arc word
        allocations sum toward the target_word_count. These are estimates, not
        prose.
    The harness will check this plan for: premise consistency, a clear central
    conflict, a defined ending target, complete arc coverage from start to ending,
    and that every major promise has an intended payoff. Make those elements
    explicit and self-consistent.
  </planning_objective>

  <context>
    <genre>{{ genre }}</genre>
    <target_word_count>{{ target_word_count }}</target_word_count>
    <premise_seed>{{ premise_seed }}</premise_seed>
    <world_rules>
    {% for rule in world_rules %}
      - {{ rule }}
    {% else %}
      (none provided)
    {% endfor %}
    </world_rules>
    {% if existing_arcs %}
    <existing_arcs note="Continuation pass: extend the story beyond these without contradicting them.">
      {% for arc in existing_arcs %}
      - {{ arc | tojson }}
      {% endfor %}
    </existing_arcs>
    {% else %}
    <existing_arcs>This is a fresh book; plan all arcs from the premise.</existing_arcs>
    {% endif %}
  </context>

  <compiled_constraints note="Hard requirements must be satisfied; preferences should be honored where possible. If two hard requirements truly contradict, raise_conflict instead of guessing.">
    <hard_requirements>
    {% for c in compiled_constraints.get('hard_annotations', []) %}
      - {{ c.get('text', c) }}
    {% else %}
      (none)
    {% endfor %}
    </hard_requirements>
    <preferences>
    {% for c in compiled_constraints.get('soft_preferences', []) %}
      - {{ c.get('text', c) }}
    {% else %}
      (none)
    {% endfor %}
    </preferences>
  </compiled_constraints>

  <deliberation_state>
    <turn>{{ loop_index }}</turn>
    <current_draft_plan>
    {% if current_plan %}{{ current_plan | tojson }}{% else %}(no draft yet — this is the first proposal){% endif %}
    </current_draft_plan>
    <accumulated_tool_results>
    {% for tr in tool_results %}
      - {{ tr | tojson }}
    {% else %}
      (no tools called yet)
    {% endfor %}
    </accumulated_tool_results>
    <last_validation>
    {% if last_validation %}
      {% if last_validation.passes %}The previous candidate passed all required checks.{% else %}The previous candidate FAILED these required checks — address them before finalizing: {% for fc in last_validation.failed_checks %}{{ fc }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.{% endif %}
    {% else %}
      (no validation yet)
    {% endif %}
    </last_validation>
    {% if last_refusal %}
    <refused_request note="This tool request was refused by the harness — do not repeat it.">{{ last_refusal | tojson }}</refused_request>
    {% endif %}
  </deliberation_state>

  <output_contract>
    Return EXACTLY ONE JSON object — a single PlannerAction — and nothing else: no
    prose, no markdown fence, no commentary outside the object. Choose one
    action_type and include only the fields for that action; do not add any other
    fields.

    action_type is one of:
      - "call_tool": request one read tool permitted for global-level planning
        (for example: reading existing arcs, project metadata, or world rules, or
        querying the continuity / summary stores) to inform the plan. The harness
        executes it and returns the result on the next turn; a disallowed or
        over-budget request is refused.
      - "revise_plan": submit an improved draft global plan (set revised_plan) with
        a short change_summary. Use this to build the plan up across turns.
      - "finalize_plan": submit the completed global plan as final_plan when you
        believe it satisfies every requirement above. You may include self_check,
        but it is advisory only — the harness re-runs the required checks and
        decides acceptance; a self_check is never trusted in place of them.
      - "raise_conflict": only when two HARD requirements genuinely cannot both be
        satisfied. List the conflicts (each with conflict_type, description,
        requires_user_resolution); this pauses for user clarification.

    {% raw %}
    Shape (emit only the keys for your chosen action_type):
    {
      "action_type": "call_tool" | "revise_plan" | "finalize_plan" | "raise_conflict",
      "tool_name": "<tool>",            "tool_args": { },                 // call_tool
      "revised_plan": { },              "change_summary": "<text>",       // revise_plan
      "final_plan": { },                "self_check": { },                // finalize_plan
      "conflicts": [ { "conflict_type": "<type>", "description": "<text>", "requires_user_resolution": true } ], // raise_conflict
      "rationale": "<optional short reason>"
    }

    For revise_plan/finalize_plan, the plan object should carry:
    {
      "premise": "<logline>",
      "central_conflict": "<text>",
      "ending_target": "<text>",
      "major_promises": [ { "promise": "<text>", "intended_payoff": "<text>" } ],
      "arcs": [ { "title": "<text>", "function": "<role in the story>", "word_allocation": <int> } ]
    }
    {% endraw %}
  </output_contract>

</planner_task>
